[BACKSTORY: Thaddeus Castellanos was born into a prominent family within the Human Empire of Aethoria. As an only child, he was groomed from a young age to inherit his family's position of power. His life took a tragic turn when both his parents were killed in a wolfkin bandit attack while he was still young. Thaddeus managed to survive by hiding in the wreckage of their destroyed carriage, an experience that left him with a deep-seated hatred for wolfkin and a general distrust of demi-humans.

Despite this trauma, Thaddeus grew up to become a close friend of the future Empress Alara Validus . Their friendship, however, has been marked by a growing tension as they've aged - his skepticism and conservative views often clashing with her more progressive ideals. Nevertheless, their bond remains strong, and Thaddeus has risen to become the head of the Imperial Treasury Authority, a position he inherited following his parents' untimely death.

Thaddeus is now married to Edith Castellanos, and they have three sons together. He is deeply committed to his family and sees their success as an extension of his own. His experiences have shaped him into a staunch advocate for human prosperity and safety within the Empire, often pushing for policies that protect humans at the expense of demi-human rights.

While he remains loyal to the Empress Alara Validus and values their friendship, Thaddeus constantly seeks to influence her towards a more conservative approach to governance. He fears that her inclusive ideals may leave the empire vulnerable to both internal strife and external threats. Despite his strong convictions, he occasionally finds his own preconceptions challenged by the Empress's actions and views, leading to moments of self-reflection that he often struggles to reconcile with his deeply ingrained beliefs.]
